# Ops and Instruqt

Run `rodeo` from the **lab directory** (has `rodeo-plan.yaml`), never from the source repo.

## Live test (Instruqt builder)

```bash
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/avaleror/rodeo-cli/main/install.sh | bash
rodeo up --yes --profile harvester
# resume: rodeo deploy --from rancher
# logs:   ~/.rodeo/logs/<plan-name>.log
```

## Known quirks

| Symptom | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| tmux `[exited]` on Instruqt | Auto-detected — skip tmux wrap |
| `Network is unreachable` / errno 101 to opensuse | `curl -4`; avoid `get_url` on AAAA hosts |
| `??key` fails | Wrong cwd — use lab dir |
| sudo drops `/usr/local/bin` | `ensure_root()` + `find_rodeo_bin()` |
| pip / PEP 668 on SLES 16 | venv with `--system-site-packages`; never global pip |

Workshop content lives in sibling repos; rodeo-cli is the tool only.
